Arthur “Art” Williams Jr. is a former counterfeiter known for mastering the 1996 $100 bill. After serving 12 years in prison, he is now an artist and speaker.&amp;nbsp;

Art joins Theo to talk about how he was able to counterfeit almost $10M in cash before getting caught, the paranoia that comes with a life of crime, and the best ways to spend fake money.&amp;nbsp;

